cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the exact release and, for any computation, the campaign document it used."
type: software
title: "Polyhedraproof: a checked SAT pipeline for twelve pairwise-adjacent planar faces"
authors:
  - family-names: Pirozhkov
    given-names: Andrei
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-6901-7843"
version: 1.0.0rc1
date-released: 2026-10-17
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/pirozhkov-andrei/polyhedraproof"
abstract: >-
  Whether a polyhedron with twelve pairwise adjacent planar faces exists is an open question;
  the tetrahedron and the Szilassi polyhedron are the only known polyhedra with every two
  faces adjacent. A necessary-condition SAT encoding of polyhedra with twelve pairwise adjacent planar
  faces under the accompanying article's surface and face-intersection hypotheses.
  Given the article's reduction, checked refutations of all 59 CNF formulas would prove
  nonexistence in that class. The pipeline has every refuted case checked by the verified
  LRAT checker cake_lpr.
  This release does not include, and does not claim, the completed computation.
keywords:
  - polyhedra
  - oriented matroids
  - SAT
  - LRAT
  - formal verification
# At publication: the DOI of the archived release
# (docs/RELEASE.md, "Publishing"); the article's arXiv identifier once it has one.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Twelve pairwise adjacent faces: a chirotope reduction to Boolean unsatisfiability"
    authors:
      - family-names: Pirozhkov
        given-names: Andrei
        orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-6901-7843"
    notes: "The accompanying article, paper/faces12-en.tex of this release (CC BY 4.0)."
